WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.320
- Seed of Chucky is a direct&nbsp;
sequel to Bride of Chucky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:05.200
following up on the explosive birth&nbsp;
of Chucky and Tiffany’s baby seen at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.480
the end of that movie. Like Bride, Seed&nbsp;
would continue the trend of metacinema,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:12.080
drawing our attention to horror movie tropes&nbsp;
and not being so subtle about its influences.

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:15.040
Last episode, when I talked about Bride, I&nbsp;
mentioned that this new direction for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:18.640
franchise was a direct result of the Scream&nbsp;
movies having a huge impact on our culture.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:21.680
- [Tiffany] For God sake Chucky,&nbsp;
drag yourself into the 90s!

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.200
- [Zac] ...right down to the new Chucky logo containing&nbsp;
a spike, much like the letter M in the Scream&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:28.880
logo. The new logo for Seed, which would&nbsp;
be used going forward, is slightly changed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:32.320
this time the Y is the pointy letter, making&nbsp;
it look even more like the Scream logo.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.920
The opening scene pays homage to Chucky’s&nbsp;
slasher forefather: Halloween, by showing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:40.000
scene through the point of view of the antagonist,&nbsp;
just like Halloween’s opening. But having a clear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.720
dependence on Halloween, in a way, is also another&nbsp;
example of how Chucky was influenced by Scream,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:48.080
because if you remember in the original&nbsp;
Scream, the movie they all watch at Stu’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:52.240
party is Halloween, and many of Halloween’s&nbsp;
tropes come up during the events of that party.

00:00:52.240 --> 00:01:00.151
- [Randy] Jamie, look behind you. Look behind you. Turn around. Behind you. Be-hind you!

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:04.720
- [Zac] Bride was very much galvanized by Scream 1 and 2,&nbsp;
but since then, a third Scream movie was released,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:08.640
and Seed of Chucky would look to it for further&nbsp;
inspiration. To learn how Seed of Chucky was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:12.560
a mashup of several horror concepts,&nbsp;
stick around to the end of this video.

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:14.400
This video is sponsored by Keeps.

00:01:14.517 --> 00:01:19.057
(metal music)

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:25.440
Welcome to Things You Missed. Seed of Chucky tells&nbsp;
the story of the indecisive intersex interloper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:28.640
known as either Glen or Glenda. It’s not&nbsp;
really clear which name is accurate by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:31.680
end of the movie, so I’ll just go with&nbsp;
whatever seems appropriate at the time.

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:34.720
The entire plot is set into action&nbsp;
when Glen sees the Made In Japan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:37.600
marking on his wrist that matches the&nbsp;
mark he sees on Chucky’s wrist when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:40.433
the doll appears on TV to promote&nbsp;
the movie being made about him.

00:01:40.987 --> 00:01:42.987
- [Chucky] ...ck you very much.

00:01:42.987 --> 00:01:43.861
(applause)

00:01:43.861 --> 00:01:45.249
(Glen gasps)

00:01:49.854 --> 00:01:51.600
- [Glen] I'm no orphan after all!

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:55.040
- Which is just wrong. It doesn’t make sense&nbsp;
that Chucky would have a Made In Japan mark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:59.120
because we clearly see the doll was created&nbsp;
in a factory in Chicago during Child’s Play 2&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:02.000
and Charles Lee Ray himself was&nbsp;
born in Hackensack, New Jersey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:05.280
as was Glen who was liveborn in&nbsp;
the cemetery at the end of Bride.

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:09.480
That is not going to be my only accuracy gripe,&nbsp;
but let’s get into the Things You Missed.

00:02:09.897 --> 00:02:14.202
(foreboding music)

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:18.480
After the opening dream scene, we find&nbsp;
ourselves in a graveyard, where Santa Claus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:22.240
or someone posing as him, discovers he’s been&nbsp;
giving Chucky and Tiffany a ride in his sack&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:25.920
of toys. When Chucky comes face to face&nbsp;
with the big man, he makes this discovery.

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:31.360
- [Chucky] I knew it! You’re not real!

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:35.280
- This is an ironic thing to say, because&nbsp;
throughout Chucky’s entire existence as a doll,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:38.880
he’s only been able to get away with the things&nbsp;
he does because nobody believes that he’s real,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:41.280
the majority of the public just&nbsp;
thinks he’s a regular doll.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:44.480
This whole scene ends up being part of&nbsp;
the production of a movie within the movie.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:48.080
They have to stop filming due to some technical&nbsp;
difficulties in the special effects department.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:52.240
- Chucky broke again. This is bloody ridiculous!

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:55.520
This a little nod to what famously went on&nbsp;
behind the scenes during the production of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:59.680
the 1975 horror movie Jaws, where the&nbsp;
titular shark was an animatronic that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:02.400
was constantly breaking down and&nbsp;
messing up the shooting schedule.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:04.688
- [Richard Dreyfuss] You could hear this:

00:03:04.706 --> 00:03:07.566
(static) the shark is not working. (static)

00:03:07.643 --> 00:03:09.643
Repeat, the shark is not working. 

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:14.160
- The concept of a Chucky movie being made within&nbsp;
another Chucky movie heavily derives from Scream&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:18.400
3. In each of the Scream sequels so far, Hollywood&nbsp;
makes a movie adaptation based on the events&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:22.000
of one of the previous movies, which is&nbsp;
referred to in-universe as the Stab! franchise.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:23.040
 Scream 3 features&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:26.960
actor counterparts of each major character,&nbsp;
and Seed of Chucky goes one step further,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:30.320
by casting Jennifer Tilly, who played&nbsp;
Tiffany in Bride to play herself:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:34.800
Jennifer Tilly, who is also playing the adaptation version of Tiffany in the movie within the movie.

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:37.520
Seed of Chucky must take place in a&nbsp;
world not too different from our own,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:40.320
because Jennifer mentions that she thinks&nbsp;
she should have played Erin Brockovich,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:44.400
which her rival Julia Roberts won the&nbsp;
Academy Award for Best Actress for in 2001.

00:03:45.501 --> 00:03:47.501
- And the Oscar goes to...

00:03:48.857 --> 00:03:50.720
Julia Roberts!

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:54.880
She also makes reference several times to&nbsp;
her own Oscar nomination in the 1994 film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:57.840
Bullets Over Broadway. Additionally,&nbsp;
the Variety newspaper that she reads&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.720
features real articles from the&nbsp;
world of entertainment in 2004,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:05.200
and we see a magazine later on mentioning&nbsp;
the 2004 Spanish horror film Rojo Sangre.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:09.120
Scream 3 came out in 2000 and loved to&nbsp;
parody real life stuff from Hollywood.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:13.360
But there’s another horror movie that played&nbsp;
even more of a role in influencing Seed, and we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:17.280
can find it when we look to the title of Chucky&nbsp;
movie the being shot in that second sequence.

